{
  "letter": "d",
  "title": "Tile D Charcoal",
  "name": "Charcoal",
  "blurb": "A calm work dashboard, dark first, in black, grey and white: filled cards with clear edges, round buttons and labels, and one red, #ff0000, kept for where you are, what is most urgent and what is unread.",
  "fontsHref": "https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Source+Code+Pro:wght@400&family=Source+Sans+3:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Source+Serif+4:opsz,wght@8..60,600&display=swap",
  "themeRule": {
    "default": "dark",
    "blocks": [
      ":root",
      ":root[data-theme=\"light\"]"
    ],
    "noSystemBlock": true,
    "wording": "Dark is the default. globals.css has two theme blocks: bare :root holds the dark values and :root[data-theme=\"light\"] holds the light ones. There is no @media (prefers-color-scheme) copy of either, so with no data-theme the app is dark under a light system too. Light shows only when data-theme=\"light\" is set. Auto (follow the system) is a third choice that a script resolves by setting or removing data-theme; it is never what a first visit gets.",
    "appNote": "Brief 103 already has the two blocks and no media copy. It differs in one place: there, no stored choice means Auto, so a first visit under a light system opens light. For \"dark mode default\" no stored choice has to mean Dark: resolveTheme returns dark when nothing is stored, the menu shows Dark checked, and picking Auto stores the word auto."
  },
